  dominant failure:
    lock publication witness was lost at src/csk/locking.py:344
  independent Windows behavior:
    Path.rename on the live stable lock failed with WinError 32 while its
    handle was open.

root cause:
  os.open omitted O_BINARY. Windows CRT translated LF to CRLF on write and
  CRLF back to LF on read. fstat reported physical bytes while os.read
  returned translated logical bytes, so the size-bounded witness reader
  reached EOF with one byte remaining and returned None.

references:
  https://docs.python.org/3/library/os.html#os.open
  https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/c-runtime-library/translation-mode-constants?view=msvc-170
  https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/fileapi/nf-fileapi-lockfileex

